      "A region is an area with some shared features. New England had a cold climate, rocky soil, forests, and harbors. Small farms, fishing, shipbuilding, and trade supported towns. Many Puritans wanted communities shaped by their religion, but they did not give equal religious freedom to everyone. The Mayflower Compact at Plymouth was an agreement for making and obeying community rules. Town meetings let eligible men decide local matters. Women, enslaved people, and many other residents were excluded from these decisions.",
