      "Representatives began working together",
      "A representative is chosen to speak and decide for others. The First Continental Congress met in 1774 to coordinate responses to Britain. The Second met in 1775, organized the war effort, and adopted independence in 1776. Thomas Paine’s Common Sense argued that Americans should govern themselves instead of obeying a king. The Articles of Confederation took effect in 1781 as the first national constitution, a written plan for government. The 1783 Treaty of Paris recognized U.S. independence, but creating an effective government remained a separate task.",
      "Agreeing that a country is independent does not decide how it will collect money or make laws.",
