          "Sectionalism means putting one region’s interests ahead of the whole country. John Brown’s failed 1859 raid at Harpers Ferry aimed to start an uprising against slavery. It increased fear and division. Abraham Lincoln won the 1860 election while opposing slavery’s spread into territories. South Carolina’s leaders feared for slavery and voted to secede, or leave the United States. Other states followed and formed the Confederacy. Confederate forces attacked Fort Sumter in April 1861. Slavery lay at the center of this road to war.",
